          <p>
            For a single refrigerator, a 2,000 to 2,500-watt inverter is the practical minimum. It has the surge headroom for the compressor and enough running capacity to add a freezer. Go bigger only if you want other circuits too.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Refrigerator Only</h3>

          <p>
            A 2,000-watt class inverter like the Honda EU2200i, Westinghouse iGen2550c or Champion 2500 handles the start-up surge of a typical kitchen fridge, runs it quietly at low throttle and sips fuel. This is the size for most people whose priority is simply not losing the groceries. Our <a href="/best-2000-watt-inverter-generator/">2000-watt inverter generator</a> roundup covers more options in this class.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Refrigerator and a Freezer</h3>

